# ACT II, optional: the captain's stern gallery at sundown. No puzzle and nothing needed: the
# view, a glass of rum, and Vane off duty (dialogue/gallery.adv). The cabin opens it once she
# has named her terms and shuts it when she goes up to the wheel (marrow_cabin.adv).
# Vane steps out with Fenn and back in with him: arriving here sets vane_out, arriving in the
# cabin clears it, and each room shows her only on its own side of that flag.
room marrow_gallery "The Marrow — Stern Gallery"
  bg bg_gallery_wide
  width 2560
  music music_sunset
  ambience sea
  perspective horizon 255 ref 875 height 485
  # Sit the figures in the sunset; the plate is already the right time of day.
  grade "sepia(0.14) saturate(1.04) brightness(1.02)"
  # The deck boards between the cabin doors and the captain's table. The rail is not floor,
  # and nor is anything behind the table.
  walk (525,878) (548,806) (1890,806) (1905,878)
  entry 640,842

  footsteps deck
  light 2232,80 radius 110 lantern
  light 196,211 radius 90 lamp
  water (530,270) (2180,270) (2180,525) (1100,525) (1100,460) (940,460) (940,525) (530,525) ripple 1.8
  motes glints (560,300) (2150,300) (2150,450) (560,450) count 45
  emit lapping at 1500,620
  emit creak

  # At her rail, looking out along her gallery, away from the door.
  sprite npc_vane_rum at 1700,812 size 1 flip idle speaker vane for vane grade "saturate(0.92) brightness(0.96)"

  on enter
    set vane_out

  scene if not gallery_sundown
    set gallery_sundown
    say "Sundown. The captain takes her rum out here every evening, alone. Tonight the door's on the latch. That's an invitation."

  hotspot doors "the cabin doors"
    area 190,40 330x800
    stand 600,842
    exit marrow_cabin
    look "The doors back into the cabin, lamplight through the glass. In there she's the captain. Out here she's something else."

  hotspot sun "the sunset"
    area 1110,50 320x210
    nowalk
    look "The sun is going down over the Straits with a lack of restraint that, in Port Vela, would need a permit."

  hotspot wake "the wake"
    area (1185,272) (1265,272) (1630,530) (640,530)
    nowalk
    look "Our wake, ruled straight back across the Straits to Port Vela. The neatest line I've seen since I left my desk."

  hotspot straits "the Straits"
    area (500,262) (1170,262) (630,530) (500,530)
    nowalk
    look "Three years I watched this sea from a customs window and took it for blue. It's every colour there is. It never told the harbour."

  hotspot islands "the islands"
    area 1495,208 370x60
    nowalk
    look "Islands, going blue with distance like ink drying on a page. Not one of them is on any form I've ever stamped."

  hotspot gulls "gulls"
    area 1570,0 620x135
    nowalk
    look "Gulls, hanging in the air off the stern without moving a feather. At the customs house we called that a promotion."

  hotspot fish "flying fish"
    area 945,462 150x80
    nowalk
    look "A flying fish leaves the sea, glides fifty yards on fins never meant for it, and drops back in, astonished. I know the feeling."

  hotspot rail "the rail"
    area 500,530 1480x272
    stand 1180,812
    look "The rail, carved with vines and polished by twenty years of a captain's elbows. There's a dent in it exactly the size of a glass."
    push "I lean on it, like a sailor. The sea leans back, like the sea. I stop."
    pull "It's held twenty years of the captain leaning on it. It isn't coming off for me."

  hotspot table "the captain's table"
    area 1975,590 290x290
    nowalk
    look "A bottle of rum, and a glass poured to the brim that nobody's touched. The captain has her own. This one isn't for me."
    pickup "It isn't mine to take. I get the feeling it isn't hers, either."
    state if seen:gallery.inside
      look "Pell's glass, empty, at the rail. The sea had it at dark."
    state if seen:gallery.owed
      look "Pell's glass, poured to the brim. The sea gets it at dark."

  hotspot lantern "the stern lantern"
    area 2185,0 240x190
    nowalk
    look "A brass lantern on a bracket, lit already, in case the sun changes its mind."

  hotspot carving "the carving"
    area 2385,560 175x320
    nowalk
    look "Gilt carving on the gallery corner: vines, a cherub, and a mermaid with the look of someone asked to hold a pose."

  # After the rail, so she wins where she stands in front of it.
  hotspot vane "Captain Vane"
    show if vane_out and not vane_convinced
    area 1610,340 200x470
    stand 1470,842
    look "Captain Vane at her rail, with rum and the whole sunset. Out here she looks less armoured. Slightly. Like a fort with a window box."
    talk "She doesn't turn round. She moves the bottle an inch further from me, which I take as hello."
      talk gallery
    give "“If it isn't rum or a reason, clerk, keep it.”"
    state if seen:gallery.root
      talk "She doesn't turn round. She doesn't need to."
        talk gallery at again

  use pell_log on vane
    "She closes my hand over it without looking down. “Not out here, clerk. That's a conversation for the chart table.”"
  use compass on vane
    "She doesn't look at it. “I've seen where it points, clerk. Let me look at where I've been for five minutes.”"
  use compass on wake
    "I hold the compass over the wake. The needle swings round and points back through the cabin, at the Straits. It has no interest in where we've been."
  use sextant on sun
    "I put Pell's sextant to my eye and try to bring the sun down to the horizon. It gets there before me, without any help."
  use stamp on table
    "Stamp the captain's rum PASSED, and Dorrit will want to inspect it. Then the captain will want to inspect Dorrit."
